<title>USA: AFTER THE BELL - Stocks quiet.</title>
<headline>AFTER THE BELL - Stocks quiet.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks were calm in after-hours trading in a session with no noteworthy transactions, traders said Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;It's quiet,&quot; said one.  </p>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said session one had a volume of 71,100 shares, compared to Thursday's 63,600. Session two had 80,300 against 1.22 million a day earlier.</p>
